  "result": "The fix is in. Completion now keeps arguments that contain `#`: `split_arg_string(\"cli a #b c\")` returns `[\"cli\", \"a\", \"#b\", \"c\"]` instead of dropping everything after `#b`. The full suite passes (1909 passed, 102 skipped, 1 xfailed), and `ruff check` and `ruff format --check` are clean on the touched files.\n\nChanges:\n- **`src/click/shell_completion.py`**: `split_arg_string` sets `lex.commenters = \"\"`, so shlex no longer treats `#` as a comment.\n- **`tests/test_parser.py`**: three new cases: `cli a #b c`, `cli a#b`, and `cli #`.\n- **`CHANGES.md`**: an \"Unreleased\" entry at the top, since the file had no unreleased section. Rename it if you prefer a version heading.\n\nI didn't add the `test_full_complete` case the plan mentioned, so the end-to-end path for each shell is covered only through `split_arg_string`. I also didn't commit anything. Say if you want a commit.",
